{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghsSoCsZpdHJNiBgrVpy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For d³ octahedral, the ⁴T₂ ← ⁴A₂ transition energy is 10Dq, so Dq = 2155 cm⁻¹.\n\nFor B, I use the Tanabe–Sugano expression for the two spin-allowed quartet transitions:\nν₃ + ν₂ = 30Dq + 15B − ... which is only exact in the form below.\n\nThe ⁴T₁(F) and ⁴T₁(P) states mix. The energies are the roots of the matrix\n|−6Dq... |\n\nUsing the standard result with x = 10Dq:\nE(⁴T₁(F)) = 15B + 15Dq − ½[(...)]\n\nA simpler route is the sum rule for the two ⁴T₁ levels. Their eigenvalues are\nE± = 7.5B + 15Dq ± ½√[(15B − 10Dq)² + 12B·10Dq·... ]\n\nI'll write it out explicitly. The ⁴T₁ matrix, with energies taken relative to ⁴A₂, is:\n- ⁴T₁(F): 12Dq − 12Dq... \n\nI won't derive the matrix from memory. Instead I use the known ⁴T₁(F) result.\n\nThe observed ⁴T₁(F) is at 28 500 cm⁻¹, and ⁴T₂ is at 21 550 cm⁻¹. I take the ⁴T₁(F) ← ⁴A₂ transition as ν₂, the lower of the two ⁴T₁ roots. The matrix is (zero at ⁴A₂, with Δ = 10Dq):\n- H11 = 15B + Δ... \n\nI'll run the numbers with a tool to avoid errors."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1673,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1673,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b7dadc2-0281-400c-9557-acead457bf42","uuid":"bf316d66-0102-4bc3-8372-5f4ebfcef7e9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:15:15.766Z","request_id":"req_011CghsSnp4pr82r8ZysKsCK"}
